-- Phase 3 of the NPC / bestiary work, eighth book: every species in Rifts World
-- Book 7: Underseas - its Sea Monsters of Note (printed 20-38), the Lord of the
-- Deep's minions (45-48) and the ocean's R.C.C.s (51-165) - rows for creatures
-- (migration 074) and their attacks in stat_attacks (owner_kind 'creature').
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
-- The fourteen playable rows are the races the book offers as player characters:
-- the Dragon Ray, the Rurlel Eel People, the three Pneuma-Biforms, the Dolphin,
-- Killer, Sperm and Humpback Whales, the Amphib, Sea Titan, Naut'Yll, Kreel-Lok
-- Nomad and Horune Pirate. All fourteen are already published classes;
-- these rows are the NPC view of them. The Naut'Yll is one row, its soldier,
-- devastator and koral shaper noted. Every monster and animal is an NPC.
--
-- NOT HERE: the Lord of the Deep, a named being (notable_npcs, not imported
-- yet), and its Reachers (printed p.44), which are its own limbs rather than a
-- species; the gene-splicer monsters, which are rolled on tables, not stated.
--
-- DECISIONS: Servants of the Deep are humans changed by years of service - the
-- book prints no attributes, so they roll a human's 3D6, with the bonuses by year
-- in bonuses_note. Monster Naut'Yll's M.D.C. is printed as "triple normal", so
-- it is triple the Naut'Yll's P.E.+1D4x10. The Picasso Magic Fish is an S.D.C.
-- animal whose 2D6 M.D.C. lasts only while it is charged. A speed printed only in
-- mph stays in pools_note rather than posing as a Spd attribute, and an A.R.
-- printed as dice (the whales) is in pools_note too.
--
-- A RIFTS BOOK: an M.D.C. creature's pool is its Main Body M.D.C.; the "on
-- S.D.C. worlds" figures and the M.D.C. by location are in pools_note. The
-- dolphins and whales are S.D.C. beings.
--
-- EXTRACTED by five book-extract-workers, each given the NAMES of its species,
-- every number read off a 200 dpi render of the scan. RECONCILED by book-reconcile
-- against the renders, row by row; its corrections are applied. Every row passes
-- creatureFormulaGaps, the grammar the endpoint rolls with. description and
-- natural_abilities are short paraphrases - no sentence is the book's.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-creatures-underseas.sql
--
-- BY CATEGORY:
--   monster (12): Dragon Ray, Lorica Wraith, Sea Maw, Shadow Sharks, Storm Riders,
--     Zomba, Stidjron, Devil Shark R.C.C., Monster Naut'Yll, Psiren R.C.C., Sea
--     Doppleganger, Servants of the Deep
--   animal (9): Giant Octopus, Giant Squid, Picasso Magic Fish, Great White Shark,
--     Tiger Shark, Dolphin, Killer Whale (aka Orca), Sperm Whale, Humpback Whale
--   humanoid (1): Rurlel Eel People
--   hybrid (3): Pneuma-Biform Dolphin, Pneuma-Biform Killer Whale, Pneuma-Biform Whale
--   mutant humanoid (1): Amphib
--   superhuman humanoid (1): Sea Titan
--   alien humanoid (3): Naut'Yll, Kreel-Lok Nomad, Horune Pirate

  'dragon-ray', 'Dragon Ray', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but most are scrupulous, unprincipled, or anarchist.', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+6","MA":"4D6+6","PS":"2D6+16","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"2D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx10+2D6', NULL, 'ME+6D6', 'Hit Points: Mega-damage creature (uses M.D.C. only). Spd. Underwater: 2D6+30 (roughly 22-30 mph/35-48 kmph/30-41 knots); Flying: 2D6+76. M.D.C. gains +2D6 per level of experience on top of base P.E. x10. I.S.P. gains +1D6+2 per level of experience on top of base M.E.+6D6. Can hold breath 2D4x10 minutes. Depth tolerance 1 mile (1.6 km).', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":3,"strike":3,"parry":4,"dodge":5,"roll":4,"pull":1}', 'Attacks: 3 at level one, +1 at levels three, six, nine, twelve, fifteen. +1 to save vs magic and poison, +2 vs disease, +3 vs horror factor; a natural 19 or 20 is a critical strike; P.S. is considered supernatural. Slave value: prized by some alchemists, occasionally captured and sold as slaves or pets.', 'Swim 98%, Advanced Fishing +10%, Language: Dragonese 94%, Language: two of choice +30%, Literacy: one of choice +20%, Ocean Geographic Surveying +20%, Underwater Navigation +15%, Undersea Survival +10%, Lore: Monsters and Demons +10%; plus eight R.C.C. Related Skills (one more at levels 3, 7, 11, 15) and one secondary skill at levels 1, 3, 5, 8, 11.', 'Swims 98%, flies, immune to cold, prehensile tail, heals twice as fast as humans, and regenerates lost fins, tail, or limbs in 3D4 weeks; can leap or glide from water, make sharp turns, and burst to double speed.', 'About 7% learn some form of magic; most avoid it as too demanding.', 'Major psionic: bio-regeneration (super), ectoplasm, resist fatigue, mind block, total recall, speed reading, plus two of choice from sensitive or physical.', '16 to 20 feet (4.9-6.1 m) long, wingspan 20 to 25 feet (6-7.6 m)', '600 to 900 lbs (270-405 kg)', '900 years, some as long as 3000', 'Coastlines, islands, sea cliffs, beaches, and coastal villages worldwide; splits time roughly 60/40 between sea and land', 'None per se, but likes humans, aquatic humanoid D-bees, and other friendly, intelligent beings', 'None per se', 'May instead select a magic O.C.C., using that O.C.C. skills/abilities at half the related skill selections, while staying on the Dragon Ray Experience Table.', 'A sociable, manta-ray-like mega-damage creature at home in water, air, and land, often adopted by coastal communities as a beloved storyteller.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.20-23');
  'giant-octopus', 'Giant Octopus', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered to be anarchist or evil predators.', '{"IQ":"1D6+4","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6","PS":"2D6+40","PP":"2D6+12","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D4x10+PE', NULL, NULL, 'Hit Points: Mega-damage (uses M.D.C. only). Swimming speed 15 mph (24 kmph/13 knots). Depth tolerance 3 miles (4.8 km).', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":2,"strike":4,"parry":5,"dodge":2}', 'Plus 6 to save vs horror factor; has supernatural strength. Market value: none.', NULL, 'Swims 98%, climbs 95%, prowls 70% (90% while color-hiding), sees 3000 ft at night, tastes/tracks chemicals in water, sprays a blinding ink cloud, and bio-regenerates 5D6 M.D.C. per day, regrowing lost parts in 3D4 weeks.', NULL, NULL, '50 to 60 feet (15.2-18.3 m) long', 'One ton', '90 to 120 years', 'Ocean floor worldwide; comparatively rare', 'None; lone hunters or mated pairs', 'Sperm whales; frightened humans', NULL, 'A real-world octopus grown into a mega-damage sea predator, hunting mostly at night and preyed on in turn by whales.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.23-24');
  'giant-squid', 'Giant Squid', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered to be anarchist or evil predators.', '{"IQ":"1D6+2","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+30","PP":"2D6+14","PE":"2D6+20","PB":"1D6"}', NULL, NULL, '3D4x10+PE', NULL, NULL, 'Hit Points: Mega-damage (uses M.D.C. only). Swimming speed 25 mph (40 kmph/21.5 knots). Depth tolerance unlimited.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":4,"strike":6,"parry":6,"dodge":2}', 'Plus 1 to save vs magic, +8 vs horror factor; has supernatural strength. Market value: none.', NULL, 'Swims 98%, climbs 85%, sees 3000 ft at night, sees the invisible, immune to cold, sprays an ink cloud, and bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per day, regrowing lost parts in 2D4 weeks.', NULL, NULL, '40 to 70 feet (12.2-21.3 m) long', 'One ton', '80 to 120 years', 'Oceans and seas worldwide, most common in deep, cold water', 'None; lone hunters', 'Sperm whales', NULL, 'A pre-Rifts deep-sea giant now dealing mega-damage; usually leaves humans alone, but some acquire a taste for humanoid prey.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.24');
  'lorica-wraith', 'Lorica Wraith', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil only.', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"1D6+30","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+10","PB":"1D4","Spd":"3D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+4D6x100', 'PEx5', 'ME+6D6', 'Hit Points: Mega-damage supernatural creature (uses M.D.C. only). Spd. Underwater: 2D6+30 (roughly 22-30 mph/35-48 kmph/30-41 knots); cannot fly. I.S.P. gains +1D6+2 per level of experience on top of base M.E.+6D6. Loses 100 M.D.C. per day if it cannot soak fully in water for at least two hours per day (regenerates 100 M.D.C. per two hours of soaking); speed and combat abilities halved while weakened; dies at 0 M.D.C. Can survive on land or in vacuum 2D6 days before weakening. Depth tolerance unlimited.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":3,"strike":6,"parry":9,"dodge":3,"pull":2,"roll":2}', 'Attacks: 7 (supernatural). Dodge is automatic (no melee action used). Plus 1 to save vs psionic attack and illusions, +2 vs magic, +8 vs horror factor; a natural 19 or 20 is a critical strike; considered a supernatural monster. Slave value: 50,000+ credits in good condition; teeth, bones, organs, bony armor, and claws are also separately valued.', 'R.C.C. Skills of Note: Swim 98%, Language: Demongogian 98%, language of choice 80%, Underwater Navigation 90%, Lore: Monsters and Demons 80%, Lore: Magic.', 'Eyeless; hunts by chemoreceptors, sonar, and psionics. Immune to cold, disease, and depth pressure; prehensile tail and tentacles; can learn speech; breathes air or vacuum for days but weakens without daily soaking in water.; bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. a MINUTE and regrows a lost appendage in 1D4 weeks', 'Dolphin-style ley line charged, ley line energy blast, and ley line speed doubler; plus ley-line-walker sense ley line/magic energy and read ley lines.', 'Master psionic: telepathy, presence sense, object read, sense evil, sense magic, detect psionics, deaden pain, psychic surgery (used to torture), plus one super-psionic power of choice.', '36 to 40 feet (11-12.2 m) long; tentacle arms reach 15-20 feet; tail 20-30 feet', '2.5 tons', '6000+ years', 'Lives in the sea indefinitely, found worldwide', 'May ally with other black-hearted fiends like the Stidjron, but often hunts alone or in pairs', 'A cruel monster with no regard for others; most surface dwellers and aquatic people attack it on sight', NULL, 'A cunning, sadistic bone-plated predator from the ocean world Lorica that stalks and tortures intelligent prey, sometimes posing as a captive pet.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.24-27');
  'picasso-magic-fish', 'Picasso Magic Fish', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Animal, effectively an anarchist.', '{"Spd":"20"}', '5D6', NULL, NULL, '4D6', NULL, 'P.P.E. (4D6, up to 24 points) burns off at one point every 15 minutes while digesting. Becomes a mega-damage creature (2D6 M.D.C.) only while charged with P.P.E.; otherwise defended by its 5D6 Hit Points. Depth tolerance one mile (1.6 km).', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":1,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"dodge":5}', 'Horror Factor: none. Market value: 50,000 credits per fish to alchemists and bio-wizards, but very rare and hard to catch, especially when charged.', NULL, 'Swims 98%, immune to cold; absorbs and stores ley line energy, then glows, can turn invisible, double its speed, and become mega-damage; casts an illusion of being five times larger with extra heads and fins.; tastes and identifies chemicals 86% and tracks by taste 88% up to two miles; gills only - dies 3D6x10 minutes out of water', 'Absorbs ley line P.P.E.; while charged can bio-regenerate, turn invisible (1D4 melee rounds), swim at double speed, +3 save vs magic, and become mega-damage (2D6 M.D.C.); creates an illusion in the style of a Picasso painting to frighten predators.', NULL, 'Two feet (0.6 m) long', '10 lbs (4.5 kg)', '20 years', 'Near ley lines in oceans and seas worldwide', 'None', 'Natural predators; humanoids', NULL, 'A small gold fish that gorges on ley line energy, glowing and casting a monstrous illusion of itself to scare off predators.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.27');
  'sea-maw', 'Sea Maw', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Effectively anarchist or evil; a predator.', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"1D6+60","PP":"1D6+12","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D4","Spd":"1D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx1000', NULL, NULL, 'Hit Points: Mega-damage creature (uses M.D.C. only). I.Q. is qualified as low animal intelligence. Cannot fly or function on dry land. Each fin is approximately 70 M.D.C. on top of the P.E. x1000 base. Depth tolerance unlimited. Can breathe air for only 30 minutes before dying.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"strike":2,"dodge":1,"roll":3}', 'Dodge bonus has no matching parry bonus. Plus 2 to save vs magic and mind control, +8 vs horror factor (too blind and stupid to be afraid). Considered to have supernatural strength and endurance. Market value: 150,000+ credits alive or recently slain; skin can be treated into 60 M.D.C. leather armor/wetsuits (blunt, explosive, impact attacks still do half damage to the wearer); untreated skin quickly rots.', NULL, 'Swims 98%; immune to cold, disease, poison, and depth pressure; regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per melee round and regrows lost limbs in 1D4 weeks. Poor, near-sighted body-eyes see only shapes and light but work in total darkness; hunts largely by taste/smell.', NULL, NULL, '70 to 100 feet (21.3-30.5 m) long; mouth 20-30 feet (6.1-9.1 m) in diameter', '80 tons or more', '1000+ years', 'Oceans and seas worldwide', 'None per se', 'None per se, though some pirates, whalers, and minions of Splugorth hunt them', NULL, 'A huge, dim-witted gulper that swallows prey whole by mistake as often as on purpose, and can be cut open from inside its stomach.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.28-29');
  'great-white-shark', 'Great White Shark', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist or evil predator', '{"IQ":"1D6+1","PS":"2D6+30","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+20"}', '1D6x100', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Printed as "Hit Points & S.D.C. (typical): 1D6x100 total points" - one combined figure, not separated. Some ancient sharks and mutants can have 1D6x10 M.D.C. instead of the S.D.C. form. Full-strength bite is 2D6 M.D. for ancients, 5D6 M.D. for mutants (base bite below is the S.D.C. figure); tail slap is 1D6 M.D. (ancient) or 2D6 M.D. (mutant). Spd. is printed as a flat 10 mph (16 kmph/8.6 knots) swimming; typically cruises at 1-2 mph.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":3,"strike":4,"dodge":2}', '+3 save vs poison and disease, +10 save vs horror factor. Shared shark trait (see the "Sharks" intro, p.29): automatically tastes blood in the water and can be forced into an uncontrollable feeding frenzy.', NULL, 'Swims 98%, fair vision, cold-immune, nightvision 3000 ft, senses electrical fields and muscle movement with no blindness penalty in total darkness (3000 ft range), tracks blood scent, magnetic-north sense, ultrasonic probe; can survive out of water up to 2D4x10 minutes.', NULL, NULL, '20-40 ft (6.1-12.2 m) long on average; ancients/mutants to 70 ft (21.3 m)', '2-4 tons', '150 to 300 years', 'Oceans and seas worldwide; most common in the Pacific off California, Australia and Japan', 'None per se', 'None per se, though some pirates, whalers and Splugorth minions hunt them', NULL, 'Large real-world predatory shark; ancient or mutated specimens can gain a mega-damage bite and body. Hunts alone or in small groups, prone to blood-triggered feeding frenzies.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.29-30');
  'tiger-shark', 'Tiger Shark', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist or evil predator', '{"IQ":"1D6+2","PS":"2D6+20","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+20"}', '1D4x100', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Printed as "Hit Points & S.D.C. (typical): 1D4x100 total points" - one combined figure, not separated. Some ancient sharks and mutants can have 1D4x10 M.D.C. instead of the S.D.C. form. Full-strength bite is 1D6 M.D. for ancients, 4D6 M.D. for mutants; tail slap is 1D6 M.D. (ancient) or 2D6 M.D. (mutant). Spd. is printed as a flat 20 mph (32 kmph/17.2 knots) swimming; typically cruises at 1-2 mph.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":4,"strike":4,"dodge":2}', '+8 save vs poison and disease, +10 save vs horror factor. Shared shark trait (see the "Sharks" intro, p.29): automatically tastes blood in the water and can be forced into an uncontrollable feeding frenzy.', NULL, 'Swims 98%, fair vision, cold-resistant (half damage), nightvision 1000 ft, senses electrical fields/muscle movement with no blindness penalty in darkness, tracks blood scent, magnetic-north sense, ultrasonic probe; survives out of water up to 2D4x10 minutes.', NULL, NULL, '12-20 ft (3.6-6.1 m) long on average; ancients/mutants to 40 ft (12.2 m)', '1-2 tons', '100 to 200 years', 'Oceans and seas worldwide, preferring warm water; most common in the Pacific, Caribbean, Australia and Philippines', 'None; solitary hunters or small groups', 'None per se', NULL, 'Large real-world predatory shark; ancient or mutated specimens can gain a mega-damage bite and body. Slightly faster and more aggressive than the great white, hunts in small groups.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.30');
  'shadow-sharks', 'Shadow Sharks', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil, supernatural predator', '{"IQ":"1D6+6","PS":"2D6+30","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+20"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10', '5D6x10', NULL, 'Cruises at a leisurely 1-2 mph normally; full swimming speed is 40 mph (64 kmph/34.4 knots). Can survive out of water for 2D4x10 minutes, half that time in direct sunlight.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":3,"dodge":4}', '+2 save vs poison and disease, +8 save vs horror factor. Only 2 attacks per round if using magic instead of melee. Sunlight blinds it and halves its combat bonuses; fire, lasers and plasma do double damage; magic and magic weapons do full damage.', NULL, 'Resembles a huge dark-grey tiger shark that can turn invisible in shadow or darkness; swims 98%, sees in the dark 3000 ft, is cold-immune, bio-regenerates 3D6 M.D. per melee round, can speak, and tracks blood scent for miles.', '5D6x10 P.P.E.; knows black water, change current, sonic blast, water pulse, tongues, plus 1D4 additional ocean magic spells of choice', NULL, '40 ft (12.2 m) long on average', '3 tons', 'Immortal', 'Oceans and seas worldwide', 'Other shadow sharks and creatures of evil, including the Lord of the Deep, demons and the Stidjron', 'None per se', NULL, 'Invisible-in-darkness supernatural relative of the tiger shark that hunts sea mammals and humanoids in pairs or small packs, exposed and weakened only by direct light.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.31');
  'storm-riders', 'Storm Riders', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Always miscreant or diabolic', '{"IQ":"2D6+6","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+12","PP":"2D6+12","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D4"}', NULL, NULL, '4D4x10+PE', '3D6x100', NULL, 'M.D.C. doubles at ley lines or in magic triangles and triples during ley line storms. Also called "Ley Line Beasts." Bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D. per melee round and regrows lost body parts within 1D4 hours. Spd. covers underwater, flying and land movement alike (40 mph/64.3 kmph/34.4 knots).', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":6,"parry":3,"dodge":3}', '+1 save vs magic, +12 save vs horror factor. Only 2 attacks per round if using magic instead of physical attacks. Fire/plasma, rune and holy weapons, Millennium Tree weapons, dragons and other creatures of magic inflict double damage on it.', NULL, 'Swims, flies, climbs 75%, sees in the dark 1000 ft and sees the invisible, is cold/poison/disease-immune, breathes without air indefinitely, and doubles its own M.D.C./speed/damage/magic on ley lines or in magic triangles.', '3D6x100 P.P.E.; knows all spell magic levels 1-3 plus repel animals, ley line transmission, energy disruption, call lightning, wind rush, life drain, dispel magic barrier, tongues, and 10 ocean magic spells of choice, all cast as a 6th level wizard', 'None, but impervious to psionic probes, mind control, telepathy, empathy, mind bond, mind wipe and illusions', '10-12 ft (3.0-3.6 m) long', '800 lbs (362 kg)', 'Immortal, but can be destroyed', 'Oceans and seas worldwide, but most common in magic triangles and near ley lines; has also appeared over Lake Michigan', 'None per se; occasionally joins forces with other evil/chaotic beings, including Lorica wraiths and shadow sharks', 'All life forms, especially those of good alignment or dedicated to peace and order', NULL, 'Supernatural entity that manifests during ley-line storms at sea to feed on P.P.E. and inflict terror; flies, swims and fights with claws, bite and minor elemental-style magic.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.31-33');
  'zomba', 'Zomba', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Effectively anarchist or evil predator', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"2D6+12","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"4D6+10","PB":"1D4","Spd":"1D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '260', NULL, NULL, 'Also called the Silicon Sea Snake. The formula printed in the book is "P.E. number x10 plus 10 points for every foot (0.3 m) of length," averaging around 260 M.D.C.; 260 is used here as the nearest typical-adult figure. I.Q. is printed as "2D6 (animal)" - modest animal intelligence but lazy and resourceful. Spd. covers underwater and land movement, roughly 9 mph (14 kmph/7.7 knots); cannot fly. Flees if M.D.C. drops below half or if the pack leader flees; hunts in groups of 1D4+2.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"strike":5,"dodge":2,"roll":3}', '+1 save vs magic, +10 save vs horror factor; no parry bonus.', NULL, 'Legless, stone-skinned sea predator; swims 98%, is cold-immune, bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D. per day and regrows lost body parts in 2D4 days, has camouflaged wound patches and tiny near-invisible eyes, and breathes air for up to 1D4 days before weakening.', NULL, NULL, '10-20 ft (3.0-6.1 m) long; mouth about 3 ft (0.9 m) across', '800 lbs (362 kg)', '150 years', 'Oceans and seas worldwide', 'None per se, though some pirates, slavers and Splugorth minions keep them as pets and guard animals', 'None per se', NULL, 'Stone-skinned, legless sea predator resembling a giant caterpillar; boards ships to devour cargo, slaves or crew, and is easily bribed with food despite its laziness.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.33-34');
  'stidjron', 'Stidjron', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic, miscreant or anarchist', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"5D6+8","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"4D6+6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"2D6+20"}', NULL, NULL, '3D4x10+60', NULL, 'MEx3', 'M.D.C. by location: fingernail blades/claws (8; 4 per hand) 30 each, head tentacle (1) 25, fins (7) 50, head/maw 100; Main Body 3D4x10+60 is used as the formula. P.S. is superhuman and inflicts mega-damage. Swimming Spd. is roughly 15-22 mph (4.6-6.6 kmph or 13-19 knots).', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":5,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"roll":3}', '+8 save vs horror factor. Completely blind (no eyes); fights entirely by psionics, echo-location and chemoreceptors. Sharks never attack Stidjron and often follow their hunting parties in an apparent symbiotic bond.', NULL, 'Blind, eyeless deep-abyss humanoid predator; swims 98%, has underwater navigation/hunting/survival skill of 90% each, is cold- and poison-immune, heals 3x faster than humans, regrows lost limbs in 2D4 months, and lures prey with a luminous, prehensile antenna-tentacle.', NULL, 'Presence sense, sense evil, sense magic, sixth sense, empathy', '25-33 ft (7.6-10 m) long from head to tail tip; antenna and arms each about 15 ft (4.6 m), body bulk about 15 ft (4.6 m)', 'One ton', '300 years', 'Oceans and seas worldwide, most plentiful in the Pacific, usually beyond two miles (3.2 km) depth; groups of 2D4, pairs or solitary; communities rarely exceed 30, fewer than 40,000 exist worldwide', 'Some associate with or serve the Lord of the Deep, pirates, and other supernatural evil beings', 'Most life forms, including humans, naut''ylls, amphibs, Lemurians, eel people, dolphins and cetaceans; hates gene-splicers though it is not their creation', NULL, 'Blind, eyeless abyssal predator with a luminous lure-tentacle and blade-like claws; hunts humans and sea life for sport, and keeps sharks as tolerated, fed companions.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.35-36');
  'rurlel-eel-people', 'Rurlel Eel People', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any (approx. 15% scrupulous, 35% unprincipled, 20% anarchist, 30% other)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"4D6+6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6+30"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+2D4x10', NULL, NULL, 'Swimming Spd. is roughly 22-30 mph (35-48 kmph or 30-41 knots) underwater or on the surface. Can only breathe air for 4D4 minutes before choking, unless special breathing equipment is used.', NULL, 9, '{"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"roll":2}', '+4 save vs horror factor. Hand to Hand: Expert (grants additional attacks per round and bonuses by level, not printed as a flat attacks number here).', 'Swim 98%, Advanced Fishing +10%, Marine Biology +10%, Language: Native Tongue 94%, Language of Choice +10%, Ocean Geographic Surveying +20%, Track & Hunt Sea Animals +10%, Underwater Navigation +15%, Undersea Survival +15%, W.P. Harpoon Gun, W.P. two of choice, Hand to Hand: Expert; plus seven R.C.C. Related Skills (mostly "Any" by category) and secondary skills at later levels.', 'Humanoid D-bee with an eel-like tail (75% of body length); swims 98%, resists cold (half damage), heals twice as fast as humans, and regenerates lost fins, tail and limbs within 4D4 months.', '10% of Rurlel are Ocean Wizards rather than warriors (Ocean Wizard O.C.C., described in the magic section)', NULL, 'Upper torso human-sized; overall length 25 ft (7.6 m), 75% of which is tail', '400 lbs (180 kg)', '100 years', 'South Pacific along the continental shelf of Chile and Peru, but can be found worldwide', 'None per se; keep to themselves, and most surface dwellers do not know they exist', 'The Lord of the Deep, his minions, and sea monsters', '10% of Rurlel may be created as the Ocean Wizard O.C.C. instead of the warrior R.C.C.', 'Peaceful, eel-tailed D-bee warrior race living off Chile and Peru; fishes and farms seaweed, avoids surface contact, and fights only to defend itself from the Stidjron and sea monsters.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.37-38');
  'devil-shark', 'Devil Shark R.C.C.', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6+4","ME":"1D6+10","MA":"1D4+4","PS":"1D6+40","PP":"1D6+20","PE":"1D6+18","PB":"1D4+1","Spd":"1D6x10"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+70', '1D6x10', NULL, 'Spd is 1D6x10 swimming underwater; can only crawl on land at a maximum Spd of 8. P.P.E. formula is for a creature considered supernatural.', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"roll":4,"pull":4}', '+4 to save vs horror factor, in addition to the combat bonuses above; all bonuses are in addition to attribute bonuses. Vulnerabilities: takes double damage from M.D. fire and plasma, as well as rune, holy and Millennium Tree weapons.; initiative: +1 (underwater)', NULL, 'Shark senses (keen hearing/smell, poor eyesight), regenerates 1D6x10 M.D.C. every 10 minutes, survives cold and ocean depths to four miles; needs no food, drink or air but is driven by blood hunger.', NULL, NULL, '12 to 30 feet long (3.6 to 9.1 m)', NULL, '25 years from the moment of the transformation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A shark fused with a human or humanoid by the Lord of the Deep''s transformation magic, retaining low intelligence and a relentless taste for flesh and blood.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.45');
  'monster-nautyll', 'Monster Naut''Yll', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6+10","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6+6","PS":"1D6+32","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx3+1D4x30', NULL, NULL, 'Spd is 6D6 underwater, 3D6 on land. M.D.C. is printed as triple a normal Naut''Yll''s (P.E. +1D4x10, printed p.148).', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":5,"parry":5,"dodge":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Six attacks per melee from tentacles, claws or bite, plus entangle and simultaneous attack; the combat bonuses above are in addition to attribute bonuses. Vulnerabilities: same as normal naut''yll, plus double damage from rune and Millennium Tree weapons.; initiative: +3 (underwater only); strike: +5 (+7 underwater); parry: +5 (+7 underwater)', 'Retains the skills it had in life, frozen at half the character''s former experience level from the moment of transformation; no new skills or growth in experience are possible (see the Naut''Yll R.C.C.).', 'Breathes air and water, nightvision 200 ft, bionic-level hearing, nine magically extending facial tentacles (to 10 ft) for ensnaring prey, regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per minute.', 'Only if the naut''yll was a magic practitioner before being transformed', 'Equivalent of mind block auto-defense; innate presence sense detecting all living things within 500 feet (152 m)', '6 to 7 feet (1.8 to 2.1 m)', '180 to 300 lbs (printed as 82 to 136 km, apparently a book typo for kg)', '40 years from the moment of transformation', NULL, NULL, 'dolphins; killer whales; humans; D-bee sailors; kreel-lok; whale singers; Lemurians; regular naut''yll', NULL, 'A naut''yll warped with barracuda traits into a cannibalistic predator, using stretching facial tentacles and razor claws to hunt former kin and other sea-dwellers.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.45');
  'psiren', 'Psiren R.C.C.', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic or miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D6+10","ME":"1D4+10","MA":"1D4+6","PS":"2D6+20","PP":"1D6+12","PE":"1D4+20","PB":"1D6+20","Spd":"2D4x10"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+3D4x10', '20+1D6', '3D4x10+40', 'Spd is 2D4x10 underwater, 3D4 on land. Horror Factor (12) applies only once its carnivorous nature is revealed.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"roll":2,"pull":2}', '+6 to save vs horror factor, +3 to save vs disease, in addition to the combat bonuses above; all bonuses are in addition to attribute bonuses. Vulnerabilities: can only crawl on land, takes double damage from rune and Millennium Tree weapons, and all bonuses are halved on dry land.', 'Speaks 1D4 languages known before transformation and selects six secondary skills from the Vagabond O.C.C.; no new skills or growth in experience are possible.', 'Supernatural attributes, no need to breathe or eat, swims 90%, dives, leaps up to 5 ft into the air, nightvision 500 ft, impervious to cold, survives ocean depths to 1.5 miles.', NULL, 'Master psionic. Empathic transmission (love/peacefulness/beauty, trust, confusion) at 10x normal range (600 ft), though victims still get a save; plus hypnotic suggestion, mind bolt, psi-sword, mind block, empathy, telepathy, and 1D4 powers of choice from the sensitive category.', '9 to 12 feet (2.7 to 3.65 m) from head to tail', '800 lbs (362 kg)', '50 years from the moment of transformation', 'Oceans and seas worldwide; occasionally freshwater lakes and rivers connected to the ocean', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A predatory mermaid-like being that lures victims with an empathic song of love and beauty before killing them with claws, teeth, or by drowning.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.46');
  'sea-doppleganger', 'Sea Doppleganger', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D6+5","ME":"1D4+8","MA":"1D4+8","PS":"4D6+6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"1D6+20","PB":"1D4","Spd":"1D6x10"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10', '20+1D6', NULL, 'I.Q. formula is described as high predatory animal intelligence. P.B. is 1D4 in its true jellyfish form, up to 20 in human guise. Spd is 1D6x10 underwater, 3D6 on land. Horror Factor (14) applies only once its true nature is revealed.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":3,"strike":3,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"roll":3}', '+3 to save vs poison and disease, +10 to save vs horror factor, in addition to the combat bonuses above; all bonuses are in addition to attribute bonuses. Vulnerabilities: triple damage from rune and Millennium Tree weapons, double damage from fire and plasma.; strike: +3 (+4 with engulf attack)', 'None. Has about as much in common with humans as real jellyfish; simply a supernatural predator.', 'Limited shapeshifting into recently killed victims or people the target knows, impervious to cold and pressure at any depth, regenerates 3D6 M.D.C. per melee round, keen shark-like sense of smell.', NULL, 'Innate, ISP-free limited telepathy to pick the shape of someone the victim knows (stopped by mind block); presence sense to 1200 ft that can tell fish from humanoids. Considered a minor psionic.', 'Varies; typically three times the size of a human in its natural jellyfish form', '100-300 lbs (45 to 136 kg)', '180 years', 'The Marianas Trench, dead pools, the Demon Sea and other dimensional triangles; encountered infrequently throughout the oceans and seas of the world', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A shapeshifting jellyfish-like predator that mimics recently killed humans or D-bees to lure and devour more victims aboard ships and coastlines.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.46-47');
  'servants-of-the-deep', 'Servants of the Deep', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic, miscreant, or anarchist', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx2', '3D6x10', NULL, 'Attributes are an ordinary human''s (3D6), the bonuses by year of service in bonuses_note; the M.D.C. is its first-year figure. The Servant begins as an ordinary human/D-bee (no attribute formula printed; Attribute Requirements: None). Before Year 1 it has ordinary hit points/S.D.C. (not given). M.D.C. and P.P.E. then grow cumulatively with years of service: Yr1 - P.E. x2 M.D.C. (replacing hit points/S.D.C.), P.P.E. +3D6x10; Yr3 - M.D.C. +2D6x10, P.P.E. +1D4x10; Yr5 - M.D.C. +50, P.P.E. +50; Yr7 - M.D.C. +50, P.P.E. +50; Yr10 (the Great Change) - M.D.C. +50, P.P.E. +100; Yr15 - M.D.C. +50, P.P.E. +50. Energy upkeep is a minimum of 20 P.P.E. per week (50 P.P.E. per week from Year 15), drawn from the P.P.E. of a dying being (animals will do in a pinch).', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Cumulative bonuses by years of service (all bonuses are cumulative): Yr1 - supernatural strength, 4 spells from levels 1-3 (ocean magic/songs excluded, cast as if by a 5th level magician), a greenish-blue Sign of the Deep mark appears; Yr3 - +6 P.S. and P.E., 4 more spells levels 1-4; Yr5 - 6 spells levels 1-5, loses body hair, skin grays/coarsens, -4 P.B.; Yr7 - 4 spells levels 1-6, boils/warts appear, -1/2 P.B., inhuman rasping voice, glowing eyes when angered, cannibalistic urges begin; Yr10 (the Great Change) - +6 P.S., arms/legs become tentacles doing 1D6 M.D. plus supernatural hand to hand damage and P.S. bonus, +200 lbs, Spd -6 on land but swims at 5D6, holds breath 4D6 minutes, survives depths to 500 ft, loses speech (grunts/groans/howls only), 4 spells levels 1-8; Yr15 - grows a foot and +200 lbs, swim Spd +10, holds breath +20 minutes, survives depths to 2000 ft, 4 more spells levels 1-10; Yr20 - compelled to leap into the ocean and is devoured, body and soul, by the Lord of the Deep.', 'Skills come from whichever O.C.C. the character had before becoming a Servant (any O.C.C.), frozen at that experience level; half are forgotten by Year 10, and only about 15 percent are remembered by Year 20.', 'Gains supernatural strength and escalating M.D.C., magic spells, and physical mutation (tentacle limbs, leathery hide, cannibalistic hunger) the longer it serves, ending in forced suicide into the Lord of the Deep at Year 20.', 'Gains spells chosen from levels 1-10 (ocean magic and songs excluded) as years of service accrue, always cast as if by a 5th level magician; see bonuses_note for the year-by-year schedule.', '60% have minor psionics, 20% major, 10% master (mind melters or mind bleeders), 10% are mystics; at least minor psionic ability is required. Their non-Servant cult followers usually have no psychic ability.', NULL, NULL, 'Service is for life once begun; the Servant is compelled to join and be devoured by the Lord of the Deep in its 20th year', NULL, 'the Lord of the Deep; the Cult of the Deep', 'Sea Inquisitors', NULL, 'Human or D-bee cultists granted escalating supernatural power and spells by the Lord of the Deep, mutating over decades into monstrous, cannibalistic tentacled beings.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.47-48');
  'pneuma-biform-dolphin', 'Pneuma-Biform Dolphin', 'hybrid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but 70% scrupulous or unprincipled; diabolic/miscreant almost unknown', '{"IQ":"3D6+3","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+6","PS":"4D6+6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"3D6+6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+2D6x10', 'PE+3D6x10', NULL, 'MDC +2D6/level; PPE +3D6/level. Spd 3D6+6 is human form only. Supernatural Swimming Speed (not an attribute): 1D4x10+60 underwater in dolphin form, 1D4x10+20 in dolphin combat form, 3D6+6 in human form. Psionics same as normal dolphin (see separate Dolphin R.C.C. roll table).', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"dodge":1}', '+4 save vs disease, +6 vs horror factor, +4 vs illusions/mind control, impervious to cold. Horror Factor 10 applies only in combat form. Combat (metallic silver) form also adds +10 MDC/level, +6 MD per physical hit, +1 attack, +1 initiative, +1 strike, +1 roll with impact, +2 pull punch; lasts 30 min/level, 3x/day.; attacks per melee: 4 in human form or 3 in dolphin form; 2 more via magic or psionics in either form', 'Swimming 98%, Dolphin/Whale Language 98%, one human language 98%, two languages +15%, Demon and Monster Lore +15%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +10%, Underwater Navigation +20%, Sing +15%, one W.P., Acrobatics, Hand to Hand: basic (upgradeable). 5 R.C.C. related skills +1 at levels 4/8/12; 5 secondary skills.', 'Shifts between dolphin, human, and an armored silver combat form with bonus M.D.C., damage, attacks and a horror factor; regenerates M.D.C.; keeps dolphin senses only in dolphin form; dehydrates on dry land without water.', 'Whale spellsongs (one per level from 3rd), ocean magic (one spell per level), full Dolphin R.C.C. magic and ley line abilities; +1 spell strength at levels 3, 7, 11', 'Same as the normal dolphin', '6-7.5 feet in combat form (about 20% larger than an average dolphin); see Dolphin R.C.C. for swimming form', NULL, 'At least 400 years; none has died of old age', NULL, 'Whale Singers; normal dolphins and whales; humans; sea titans; amphibs; sea inquisitors; good-aligned beings', 'Lord of the Deep and its minions; evil pneuma-biforms/rogue Whale Singers', NULL, 'A magic fusion of human and dolphin that shifts between dolphin, human, and an armored combat shape, casting whale spellsongs and ocean magic against the Lord of the Deep.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.51-53');
  'pneuma-biform-killer-whale', 'Pneuma-Biform Killer Whale', 'hybrid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but 60% scrupulous or unprincipled; rest principled or anarchist, can be evil', '{"IQ":"3D6+1","ME":"4D6+3","MA":"3D6+3","PS":"5D6+20","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"4D6+6","PB":"3D6+4","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+1D4x100', 'PE+2D6x10', NULL, 'MDC +4D6/level; PPE +2D6/level. Spd 3D6 is human form only. Supernatural Swimming Speed (not an attribute): 1D4x10+30 underwater in whale form, 1D4x10+10 in whale combat form, 3D6 in human form. Psionics same as normal killer whale (see separate Killer Whale R.C.C. roll table). Named individual: Knife Fin, a 12th-level rogue PB-killer whale, leads a horune pirate band that worships her as a god; her two offspring (4th and 7th level) are unnamed.', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":1}', '+4 save vs disease, +7 vs horror factor, +3 vs illusions/mind control, impervious to cold. Horror Factor 14 applies in combat form. Combat (glossy black metallic) form also adds +20 MDC/level, +10 MD per physical hit, +1 attack, +2 initiative, +1 strike, +2 roll with impact, +3 pull punch; lasts 30 min/level, 4x/day.; attacks per melee: 6 in human form or 5 in killer whale form; 2 more via magic or psionics in either form', 'Swimming 98%, Dolphin/Whale Language 98%, one human language 98%, one language of choice +15%, Demon and Monster Lore +15%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +15%, Underwater Navigation +15%, Sing +10%, two W.P.s, Hand to Hand: expert (upgradeable). 4 R.C.C. related skills +1 at levels 4/8/12; 4 secondary skills.', 'Shifts between killer whale, human, and an armored black combat form with bonus M.D.C., damage, attacks and a horror factor; regenerates M.D.C.; keeps orca senses only in whale form; dehydrates on dry land without water.', 'Limited: two whale spellsongs at level one, +1 per level from 2nd; ley line abilities same as the Dolphin R.C.C. but no dolphin magic; +1 spell strength at levels 4, 8, 12', 'Same as the normal killer whale', 'Males 30-40 feet, females 20-25 feet long (biform); upright fin 7-10 feet tall', '4 to 7 tons for a full-sized adult; male about twice the size of the female', 'At least 400 years; none has died of old age', NULL, 'Whale Singers; normal dolphins and whales; humans; sea titans; amphibs; sea inquisitors; good-aligned beings', 'Lord of the Deep and its minions', NULL, 'A magic fusion of human and orca, front-line Whale Singer warriors who transform into human or an armored combat form; some rogues instead prey on smaller cetaceans.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.53-55');
  'pneuma-biform-whale', 'Pneuma-Biform Whale', 'hybrid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but typically principled and scrupulous', '{"IQ":"3D6+5","ME":"4D6+3","MA":"3D6+6","PS":"4D6+20","PP":"3D6+3","PE":"4D6+6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+1D6x100', 'PE+4D6x10', 'ME+2D4x10', 'MDC formula is for Sperm whale and other large-whale biforms (+1D4x10/level); a Blue-whale biform instead uses PE+2D4x100 (+1D6x10/level); a Beaked or medium-sized-whale biform uses PE+1D4x100 (+4D6/level). Most PB-whales are their species maximum size. PPE +4D6/level. ISP +2D6/level. Spd 2D6 is human form only. Supernatural Swimming Speed (not an attribute): 1D4x10+30 underwater in whale form, 1D4x10+10 in whale combat form, 3D6 in human form.', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":1}', '+4 save vs disease, +7 vs horror factor, +3 vs illusions/mind control, impervious to cold. Combat (silver/white metallic) form also adds +20 MDC/level, +6 MD per physical hit, +1 attack, +1 initiative, +2 roll with impact, +2 pull punch, horror factor 11; lasts 30 min/level, 2x/day.; attacks per melee: 2 in human or whale form; 2 more via magic or psionics in either form', 'Swimming 98%, Dolphin/Whale Language 98%, one human language 98%, one language of choice +15%, Basic Math +15%, Demon and Monster Lore +15%, Magic Lore +10%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +10%, Underwater Navigation +15%, Sing +10% (+20% Humpback), one W.P. 5 R.C.C. related skills +1 at levels 4/8/12; 5 secondary skills.', 'Shifts between whale, human, and an armored combat form with bonus M.D.C., damage, attacks and horror factor; regenerates M.D.C.; deep-dives further than most cetaceans; dehydrates on dry land without water.', '5 whale spellsongs at level one, +1 per level from 2nd; 3 ocean magic spells (or dolphin magic) at level one, +2 ocean spells per level from 2nd; one Dolphin R.C.C. ley line ability at levels 2/6/10/14; +1 spell strength at levels 3, 6, 9, 11, 14', 'Master psionic: group mind block, 4 sensitive powers, 2 physical, 2 healing; +1 additional power (any category but super) per level thereafter', 'Varies by whale species: Blue whale 80-100 ft/120-160 tons, Sperm whale 36-66 ft/30-40 tons, Humpback 46-62 ft/35-40 tons, Gray whale 39-47 ft/30-34 tons, average beaked whale 20-30 ft/4-16 tons; males about 50% larger than females; PB-whales tend to be their maximum size', 'See size (varies by whale species)', 'At least 400 years; none has died of old age', NULL, 'Whale Singers; other biforms; sea druids; ocean mages; normal dolphins and whales; humans; sea titans; amphibs; sea inquisitors', 'Lord of the Deep and its minions', NULL, 'The most magically powerful Whale Singer biform, a fusion of human and whale that leads and guides the other pneuma-biforms with spellsongs and ocean magic.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.55-56');
  'dolphin', 'Dolphin', 'animal', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually good: 45% scrupulous, 25% principled, 15% unprincipled, 10% anarchist, 5% other; diabolic/miscreant uncommon', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+10","PS":"4D6+6","PP":"3D6+10","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"3D6+6","Spd":"2D6+45"}', 'PE+6D6', '2D4x10', NULL, 'PE+2D4x10', NULL, 'HP +1D6/level. SDC +10 bonus for the Bottle-nosed dolphin. PPE (from innate ley line channeling) +1D6/level. Spd 2D6+45 is swimming speed (roughly 32-38 mph); no separate land speed is given. Psionics are not a fixed ISP pool but a roll: 01-77 none; 78-88 minor (1D4+1 healing/sensitive powers); 89-97 major (1D4+3 healing/sensitive/physical); 98-00 master (one category plus 1D4+1 super powers).', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', '+1 save vs disease, +2 save vs mind control, +4 save vs horror factor, resistant to cold (half damage). Horror Factor: none.; attacks per melee: 2, +1 at levels 2, 4, 6, 10, 14 (porpoises start with 2, large whales with 1); parry: standard, with nose or tail; dodge: +2, automatic (no melee action used)', 'Swim 98%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +20%, Underwater Navigation +10%, Undersea Survival, one human language of choice +20%. 3 R.C.C. related skills plus 2 more at levels 3/7/11/15; 1 secondary skill at levels 2/4/6/8/10/12/14.', 'Echolocation, ultrasonic probing, electromagnetic sensing of living beings and vessels, magnetic-north sense, sonic blast and sonic-stun attacks, ley line energy channeling into temporary M.D.C., and a chance of psionic powers; dehydrates and is nearly helpless out of water.', 'Innate ley line channeling (temporary M.D.C. charge, energy bolts, ley hopping, speed doubler, sense/read/transmit ley lines, faster healing); can also learn 2 Dolphin spells at level one, +1 at levels 2/4/6/8/10/12/14', '01-77 none; 78-88 minor (1D4+1 healing/sensitive); 89-97 major (1D4+3 healing/sensitive/physical); 98-00 master (one category plus 1D4+1 super)', '5-7 feet long for most; 6-8 feet for the Bottle-nosed dolphin and Pygmy killer whale; 8-20 feet for other toothed whales in the dolphin family', '150-300 lbs (add 100 lbs for the Bottle-nose dolphin and Pygmy killer whale)', '50 to 100 years', 'Found worldwide', 'humans (bonds easily, especially the trained or telepathic); other dolphins and cetaceans', NULL, NULL, 'The ordinary Rifts Earth dolphin: a playable S.D.C. animal race with echolocation, sonic attacks, ley line sensitivity and a chance of psionic power.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.77-80');
  'killer-whale', 'Killer Whale (aka Orca)', 'animal', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually good: 45% scrupulous, 25% principled, 15% unprincipled, 10% anarchist, 5% other; diabolic/miscreant uncommon', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"3D6+10","MA":"3D6+10","PS":"4D6+6","PP":"3D6+10","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"3D6+6","Spd":"2D6+14"}', 'PE+4D4x10', '4D6x10', NULL, 'PE+1D6x10', NULL, 'HP formula is for a full-grown male (+10/level); females and young use PE+1D4x10 (+10/level). SDC formula is for a full-grown male; females/young use 2D6x10. PPE (from innate ley line channeling) +2D6/level. Spd 2D6+14 is swimming speed (roughly 12-16 mph). Psionics are a roll, not a fixed ISP pool: 01-77 none; 78-88 minor (1D4+1 physical/sensitive); 89-97 major (1D4+3 healing/sensitive/physical); 98-00 master (one category plus 1D4+1 super). Natural A.R. 1D4+3, rolled once.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":3,"dodge":1,"roll":1,"pull":3}', '+2 save vs mind control, +6 save vs horror factor, resistant to cold (half damage).; attacks per melee: 3, +1 at levels 2, 5, 7, 10, 13; parry: standard, with nose or tail', 'Swim 98%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +20%, Underwater Navigation +10%, Undersea Survival +10%, one human language of choice +15%. 3 R.C.C. related skills plus 1 more at levels 3/7/11/15; 1 secondary skill at levels 2/7/12/14.', 'Echolocation, ultrasonic probing, electromagnetic sensing, magnetic-north sense, family recognition, and ley line energy channeling into temporary M.D.C.; only cetacean that hunts warm-blooded prey; dehydrates and is nearly helpless out of water.', 'Innate ley line channeling (temporary M.D.C. charge, energy bolts, ley hopping, speed doubler, sense/read/transmit ley lines, faster healing); can learn ocean magic, dolphin magic or whale spellsongs in any mix, 2 spells at level one, +1 at levels 2/4/6/8/10/12/14; +1 spell strength at levels 4/8/12', '01-77 none; 78-88 minor (1D4+1 physical/sensitive); 89-97 major (1D4+3 healing/sensitive/physical); 98-00 master (one category plus 1D4+1 super)', 'Males 25-33 feet, females 14-21 feet long; upright fin 5-7 feet tall, larger than any other whale', '2 to 5 tons for a full-sized adult; male about twice the size of the female', '60 to 100 years; reach maturity at 8-12', 'Coastal North Pacific, arctic and antarctic oceans favored, but found throughout the world oceans; an estimated 11 million on Rifts Earth', 'sea titans; True Atlanteans; psi-stalkers; kittani; changelings; ogres; elves; dwarves; dog boys; wolfen; simvan; Lemurians; befriended humans', 'naut yll; horune; gene-splicers and their mutants; sea monsters; Lord of the Deep minions; demons; gargoyles/gurgoyles; lizardmen; kydians; most Minions of Splugorth', NULL, 'Rifts Earth orca: a playable S.D.C. giant dolphin, loyal to befriended humans but hostile to most aquatic D-bees and never known to kill a human.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.85-88');
  'sperm-whale', 'Sperm Whale', 'animal', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually good: 35% scrupulous, 10% principled, 20% unprincipled, 25% anarchist, 10% other', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+10","MA":"2D6+6","PS":"4D6+34","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+10","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6+16"}', 'PEx20', '6D6x10', NULL, 'PE+4D4x10', 'MEx2', 'HP formula is for a full-grown male, +20/level; females/young use PEx10, +20/level. SDC formula is for a full-grown male; females/young use 3D6x10. PPE (from innate ley line channeling) +10/level. Spd 2D6+16 is swimming speed (roughly 12-17 mph; 5x faster diving). Psionics roll (all Sperm whales have some power): 01-60 minor (MEx2 ISP, +1D6/level; see aura, see the invisible, sense magic, mind block only); 61-80 major (MEx3, +1D6+2/level; adds 1D4+1 physical or sensitive); 81-90 major (MEx4, +1D6+2/level; adds 1D4+2 healing/physical/sensitive); 91-00 master (MEx8, +2D6/level; 12 powers from any lesser category at level one, +1/level including super). Natural A.R. 2D4+6, rolled once.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":1,"initiative":1,"strike":3,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"roll":3,"pull":1}', '+4 save vs poison/disease/parasites, +1 save vs mind control, +8 save vs horror factor, impervious to cold (no damage).; attacks per melee: 1, +1 at levels 2, 4, 7, 10, 13; parry: +1, with nose or tail', 'Swim 98%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +10%, Underwater Navigation +20%, Undersea Survival +20%, one human language of choice +5%. 4 R.C.C. related skills plus 1 more at levels 3/7/11/15; 1 secondary skill at levels 2/7/12/14.', 'Deepest-diving cetacean (down to 2-3 miles), longest breath-holding, impervious to cold, chemical taste-tracking, echolocation, magnetic-north sense, family recognition, and innate ley line channeling into temporary M.D.C.', 'Limited innate ley line channeling (charge, energy blast, speed doubler, rejuvenation only); knows the basics of whale spellsongs: 3 at level one, +1 at levels 3/5/6/7/8/10/12/14; +1 spell strength at levels 4/8/12', 'All Sperm whales have psionic power; see pools_note for the roll table', 'Males 60-70 feet, females 38-45 feet long', '50-70 tons for a full-sized male; 15-30 tons for a full-sized female', '50 to 80 years; reach maturity between 11 and 16', 'North Pacific, North Atlantic, arctic and antarctic oceans favored, but found throughout the world oceans; an estimated 650,000 on Rifts Earth, not counting Pygmy or Dwarf sperm whales', NULL, 'horune pirates and whalers who hunt them', NULL, 'The deep-diving giant of Moby Dick fame: a playable S.D.C. whale that rams and drags down attackers but never strikes first.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.88-90');
  'humpback-whale', 'Humpback Whale', 'animal', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually good: 50% scrupulous, 15% principled, 15% unprincipled, 10% anarchist, 10% other', '{"IQ":"2D6+6","ME":"2D6+10","MA":"2D6+10","PS":"3D6+30","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+10","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6+14"}', 'PEx10', '5D6x10', NULL, 'PE+4D4x10', 'MEx2', 'HP formula is for a full-grown male; females/young use PEx8; book gives a single plus 10 per level of experience without specifying if it applies to both. SDC formula is for a full-grown male; females/young use 3D6x10. PPE (from Magic Abilities) +20/level. Spd 2D6+14 is swimming speed (roughly 12-16 mph). Psionics roll (all Humpbacks have some power): 01-90 minor (MEx2 ISP, +1D6/level; see aura, sense magic, mind block, plus one sensitive power); 91-00 major (MEx3, +1D6+2/level; adds two healing/sensitive powers). Natural A.R. 1D6+5, rolled once.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":1,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"roll":2,"pull":1}', '+2 save vs poison/disease/parasites, +2 save vs mind control, +5 save vs horror factor, resistant to cold (half damage).; attacks per melee: 1, +1 at levels 2, 5, 8, 11, 14; parry: +1, with nose or tail', 'Swim 98%, Track and Hunt Sea Animals +5%, Underwater Navigation +20%, Undersea Survival +10%, one human language of choice +5%. 3 R.C.C. related skills plus 1 more at levels 3/7/11/15; 1 secondary skill at levels 3/8/12/15.', 'Master singer among cetaceans, songs audible up to about 116 miles; baleen filter-feeder; echolocation; magnetic-north sense; family recognition by song; innate ley line channeling into temporary M.D.C.', 'Master of spellsongs: 4 at level one, 2 at level two, +1 per level from 3rd; limited innate ley line channeling (charge, energy blast, speed doubler, rejuvenation only); +1 save vs magic, +6 save vs whale spellsongs, +1 spell strength at levels 2/5/8/12', 'All Humpback whales have psionic power; see pools_note for the roll table', 'Males 60-70 feet, females 40-48 feet long', '60-70 tons for a full-sized male; 30-40 tons for a full-sized female', '70 to 100 years; reach maturity between 11 and 13', 'North Pacific, North Atlantic, arctic and antarctic oceans favored, but found throughout the world oceans', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The most musically gifted whale, a filter-feeding baleen giant whose complex songs make it the leading Humpback among Whale Singer mystics.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.90-92');
  'amphib', 'Amphib', 'mutant humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but most tend to be good or selfish', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"4D6","PS":"3D6+12","PP":"4D6","PE":"4D6","Spd":"3D6"}', 'PEx2', '3D6x10', NULL, '3D6', NULL, 'P.B. is not a flat formula; it varies 1D6-3D6 by an appearance roll table (Perfect Human 3D6, Webbed Hands/Feet 3D4, Frog Skin 2D6, Fish Face 2D4, Scaly Skin 2D6, Scaly+Fish Face 1D6, Oversized 1D6), each also adding an underwater swimming-speed bonus (+10 to +20) beyond the base Spd 6D6 underwater, and some add S.D.C. (up to 2D4x10). Hit Points add +1D6 per level of experience. M.D.C.: by armor or magic only (no innate M.D.C.). P.P.E. 3D6 unless a magic O.C.C. is selected.', NULL, 8, '{"dodge":2,"roll":1,"pull":1}', 'R.C.C. Bonuses (underwater only): +2 to dodge, +1 to roll with impact, +1 to pull punch; in addition to skill and attribute bonuses. Horror Factor 8 is for those not used to unusual specimens.; dodge: +2 (underwater); roll: +1 (underwater); pull: +1 (underwater)', 'R.C.C. Skills: select either the Sea Wolf or Tritonian Scientist O.C.C., or any other appropriate O.C.C. (G.M.''s call); a magic O.C.C. reduces the number of available O.C.C. skills by three. Uses the Amphib R.C.C. experience table or the O.C.C. table, whichever is higher.', 'Holds breath 5D6x3 minutes (or breathes water indefinitely if gilled); doubles air supply with breathing gear; nightvision 200 ft; cold resistant; withstands depths to 1 mile plus 300 ft per level; smell/taste/hearing 4x human underwater, detecting blood/decay 1000+100 yd per level away.', 'Only if a magic O.C.C. is selected', 'Normal, same as humans', 'Human-sized; an Oversized appearance roll adds 4D6 inches to an 8 ft base height', 'Human-average; an Oversized appearance roll adds 2D6x10 lbs to a 300 lb base', '90 years', 'Tritonia (floating city) and Earth''s oceans', 'Tritonians; renegade naut''yll; dolphins; orcas; whale singers; kreel-lok; most other aquatic D-Bees', NULL, 'May select Sea Wolf or Tritonian Scientist O.C.C., or another appropriate O.C.C. (G.M.''s call); a magic O.C.C. reduces available O.C.C. skills by three.', 'Human-frog-fish hybrid mutants born of illegal genetic experiments, amphibious with a variable appearance, now integrated Tritonia citizens allied with dolphins.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.98-100');
  'sea-titan', 'Sea Titan', 'superhuman humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any; 60% principled or scrupulous, 25% selfish, 15% evil', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+12","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"4D6+4","PB":"3D6+1","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+2D4x10', '6D6', NULL, 'All physical attributes are supernatural but do not manifest until the teens (age 13+1D6); Spd is half that on land when swimming underwater. Before manifestation, Sea Titan children have S.D.C. equal to normal human P.E.+1D4x10 (plus physical skill bonuses); hit points and S.D.C. no longer apply once the character becomes an M.D.C. being. M.D.C. adds +2D6 per level of experience. Base I.S.P. is not printed; psionics are determined by percentile roll (01-18 major, 19-50 minor, 51-97 none, 98-00 master), adding 1D4x10 I.S.P. if minor or major, or 1D4x10+10 if master.', NULL, 9, '{"initiative":1}', 'R.C.C. Bonuses: +1 on initiative, +3 save vs magic, in addition to attribute and skill bonuses. Combat: as per skill (no innate attacks-per-melee figure printed). Damage is by supernatural P.S., referred to Rifts Conversion Book One p.22 rather than printed as a die here. Vulnerabilities: magic and psionics do full damage; some rune weapons do double damage; detectable by anti-supernatural detection.', 'R.C.C. Skills: Radio: Basic, Computer Operation, Detect Ambush, Demon and Monster Lore (ID only), Swimming, Pilot: Robots and Power Armor, Pilot: two of choice, Read Sensory Equipment, Language and Literacy: American 98% plus one language of choice, W.P. Energy Pistol/Rifle/Heavy, Hand to Hand: Expert (upgradeable); plus 8 O.C.C. Related Skills and a broad secondary-skill allotment. Experience table: same as the (young and ancient) dragon.', 'Never needs to breathe, drink, or eat; immune to non-supernatural poisons and toxins; supernatural strength and endurance; regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per minute; regrows lost limbs and organs in 4D6 hours; survives depths to 4000 feet; powers dormant until the teens.', 'None innately; a few older Sea Titans who left the Navy study magic', 'Twice as likely as normal to manifest psionics (01-18 major, 19-50 minor, 51-97 none, 98-00 master); see pools_note for I.S.P.', 'As a normal human (no kinship to mythical giant Titans)', NULL, 'Unknown; no noticeable aging in almost 300 years; G.M. Note suggests up to 100,000 years, like a godling', 'New Navy vessels, Refuge and Salvation Bases, and the world''s oceans', 'New Navy (Marines, SEALs); Refuge and Salvation Bases; Tritonia (trade); True Atlanteans and other adventuring companions', NULL, 'Over 250 years old may take a second O.C.C.; all prior skills freeze, the new O.C.C. skills advance at double the normal experience cost, and it rarely exceeds 5th level.', 'Mega-damage descendants of pre-Rifts sailors mutated by a ley line accident; look human until puberty, then gain supernatural strength, endurance, and near immortality.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.113-115');
  'nautyll', 'Naut''Yll', 'alien humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but lean towards aberrant evil (about 50%)', '{"IQ":"4D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+8","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+4","PB":"2D6","Spd":"6D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+1D4x10', NULL, NULL, 'Spd is 3D4 on land (attributes above use the underwater figure, 6D6+10); marked as supernatural strength and endurance. M.D.C. species: no S.D.C. or hit points given; M.D.C. adds +1D6 per level of experience. P.P.E. is printed only as Standard, with no formula. Horror Factor is 11 for naut''yll mages and mind melters (vs base 8). Vulnerabilities: dehydrate outside water; die in 1 week unwetted or 24 hours with no water at all; -10% speed/skills after 12 hours dry; a further -20% speed/skills, -1 attack, and -50% combat bonuses after another 12 hours; lose 2D6 M.D.C. per day after that (doubled in hot, dry climates); bathing 1-2 hours per 12 hours prevents the damage. Take double damage from rune and Millennium Tree weapons and from magical heat, fire, and plasma; half damage from cold-based magic. Beyond 2 miles depth (2.5 miles in Korallyte armor): 1D6x10 M.D. per 200 ft over the limit every 5 minutes, and -50% to skills, speed, combat bonuses, and attacks while there. VARIANT O.C.C.s (same base R.C.C. stats above, plus): Soldier adds +1D4x10 M.D.C. and +1 attack per melee. Devastator (Special Forces) adds +1D6x10 M.D.C., +2 initiative, +3 save vs horror factor, +1 attack per melee, and is usually magic or psionic (30% mystic, 10% ley line walker, 10% ocean wizard, 5% shifter, 5% techno-wizard, 20% major psionic, 10% mind melter, 10% other). Koral Shaper requires I.Q. 12+ and has psionic Korallyte shaping (5 I.S.P. per 10 lbs/20 M.D.C. shaped), symbiotic living Korallyte armor (15-150 M.D.C., typically 40-80) that can form claws or blades (2D4-3D6 M.D.), spikes (1D4 M.D. each), living whips (1D6 M.D. per level), or energy blasts (1D4 M.D. per M.D.C. burned, max 15); P.P.E. 3D6x10+P.E., +10 per level; I.S.P. 2D6x10+M.E., +2D6 per level; starts with 6 spells (levels 1-6) plus Shape Koral and Koral Blast, +1 new spell per level; and 6 psionic powers (any non-super category) +1 per level.', NULL, 8, '{"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":2,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Bonuses are underwater only, in addition to skill and attribute bonuses. Horror Factor 11 for mages and mind melters.; initiative: +2 (underwater only); strike: +1 (underwater only); parry: +1 (underwater only); dodge: +2 (underwater only); roll: +2 (underwater only); pull: +2 (underwater only)', 'O.C.C.s: Soldier, Devastator, and Koral Shaper are detailed as variants (see pools_note); also mind melter, operator, wilderness scout, vagabond, or a magic O.C.C. (20% ley line walker, 20% techno-wizard, 20% warlock (mostly water/earth), 10% shifter, 5% mystic, 20% koral shaper, 5% exotic disciplines). Uses the Naut''Yll Undersea Soldier table or the appropriate O.C.C. table, whichever is higher.', 'Breathes air and water indefinitely; nightvision 300 ft; bionic-level hearing; regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per 6 hours; regrows small parts in 1D6 weeks, a hand or foot in 2D4 months, a limb or eye in 4D4 months; half damage from cold; survives to 2 miles depth (2.5 in Korallyte armor).', '20% ley line walker, 20% techno-wizard, 20% warlock (mostly water/earth), 10% shifter, 5% mystic, 20% koral shaper, 5% exotic disciplines (temporal magic, diabolism, etc.)', '01-10% minor, 11-24% major, 25-30% master (natural mind melter), 31-50% mystic (magic and psionics); otherwise none', '6 to 7 feet (1.8-2.1 m)', '150 to 300 lbs (67.5-135 kg)', '120 Earth years', 'Continental shelves and shallow ocean waters, 100-3000 miles from land; comfortable above 3300 ft depth', 'mostly only their own species; Brodkil Empire (overtures by the North Atlantic city); the Angel of Death (overtures by the North Atlantic city)', 'nearly all other species, called H''Keezh (outsider/enemy); kreel-lok (enslaved in large numbers); humans', 'O.C.C.s: Soldier, Devastator (Special Forces), and Koral Shaper detailed as variants; also mind melter, operator, wilderness scout, vagabond, or a magic O.C.C. per the percentages in pools_note.', 'Aberrant, militaristic amphibious aliens with tentacled, tripod-eyed faces; minor supernatural M.D.C. beings ruling underwater warrior-nations hostile to nearly all outsiders.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.148-152');
  'kreel-lok-nomad', 'Kreel-Lok Nomad', 'alien humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually good', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"5D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+1D6x10', '2D6', NULL, 'Spd is 1D6 on land (crawling); attributes above use the underwater figure, 5D6+6. Supernatural strength and endurance noted. M.D.C. species: no S.D.C. or hit points given; M.D.C. adds +1D6 per level of experience. Out of water (unless magic is used): -1 to strike and parry, -2 to dodge; they dehydrate 10 times faster than the naut''yll and take double damage from fire/heat out of water.', NULL, 15, '{"strike":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+1 to save vs poison; +2 to save vs horror factor (natural ability); +3 to save vs disease, pollution, and toxins (special healing trait). All in addition to skill and attribute bonuses.', 'R.C.C. Skills: Swimming 98%, Basic Math, Advanced Fishing, Sea Holistic Medicine (females only), Track and Hunt Sea Animals, Underwater Navigation, W.P. Spear. O.C.C.s: typically vagabond nomad (30%) or wilderness scout (40%) with underwater equivalencies; also priest, shaman/healer, or sorcerer (2% ley line walker, 2% whale singer, 2% mystic with ocean magic, 5% water warlock, 5% ocean wizard); high-tech O.C.C.s, skills, and equipment are not appropriate.', 'Heals 5D6 M.D.C. per hour with little scarring; regrows fins and webbing in 2D6 weeks; +3 to save vs disease/poison/toxins; survives to 4 miles depth; nightvision 1000 ft; keen smell and taste; tracks by scent 80%; breathes water, limited air breathing.', 'Per O.C.C. only (some are ley line walkers, water warlocks, ocean wizards, or mystics)', 'Standard (same as humans)', '6 to 8 feet long (1.8-2.4 m)', NULL, '100 years', 'Nomadic ocean-wide pods of 10-100 (large communities 1,000-100,000); shipwrecks, caves, reefs, and towed underwater barges; no permanent dwellings', 'dolphins; whale singers; amphibs; trustworthy surface dwellers and aquatic D-bees', 'naut''yll (enslavers; almost 40% of kreel-lok are slaves); the Splugorth/Lord of the Deep (occasional enslavers); surface dwellers who fear, hunt, or kill them', 'Typically vagabond nomad or wilderness scout O.C.C.s (underwater equivalents); also priest, shaman/healer, or sorcerer variants (ley line walker, whale singer, mystic, water warlock, ocean wizard); high-tech O.C.C.s are not appropriate.', 'Peaceful, primitive fish-armed aliens Rifted to Earth, living in nomadic ocean pods; often mistaken for Devil Sharks and increasingly enslaved by the naut''yll.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.152-153');
  'horune-pirate', 'Horune Pirate', 'alien humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Anarchist (40%), aberrant (30%), other (30%, mostly evil)', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"2D6+4","MA":"2D6+4","PS":"3D6+10","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"4D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+1D4x10', NULL, 'MEx5', 'Spd 4D6+10 applies underwater and on land equally. Considered to have supernatural strength and endurance. M.D.C. species: no S.D.C. or hit points given; M.D.C. adds +1D6 per level of experience, and they may also wear M.D.C. body armor or use magic. P.P.E. is printed only as Standard, with no formula. I.S.P. adds +1D6+2 per level of experience on top of the base M.E.x5. As a player character the horune is usually a loner/outcast/rogue of anarchist or unprincipled alignment; good horune are rare and avoid conflict with their own kind. 1-in-1,000 horune is instead a Ship Dreamer, a passive alien mystic shipbuilder detailed separately on the following page (not extracted here, not on the requested species list).', NULL, 10, '{"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"pull":2}', 'R.C.C. Bonuses: +4 to save vs disease, +4 to save vs horror factor, in addition to the combat bonuses and attribute/skill bonuses. Underwater only (additional): +1 initiative, +1 strike, parry, and dodge, +1 to roll with impact.', 'R.C.C. Skills: Basic Math, Pilot: Warships and Patrol Boats, Pilot: Water Scooters, Pilot: Water Skiing and Surfing, Pilot Related: Navigation, Underwater Navigation, Undersea Salvage, Undersea Survival, W.P. Knife or Sword, W.P. Harpoon Gun, W.P. Torpedo, W.P. Trident, W.P. Energy Pistol, Hand to Hand: Expert (upgradeable); plus 4 O.C.C. Related Skills with periodic additions. If a Mystic, gains the Mystic O.C.C. psionic and magic powers instead of the O.C.C. Related Skills here.', 'Swims 92%; holds breath 3D4 minutes to 500 ft depth; nightvision 500 ft; sees infrared/ultraviolet light; hawk-like distance vision (2 miles) but nearsighted up close; good hearing; regenerates 1D6 M.D.C. per hour; regrows small parts in 1D6 weeks, limbs in 2D4 months.', 'Only if a mystic (gains the psionic and magic powers of the Mystic O.C.C., Rifts RPG p.85, forgoing the O.C.C. Related Skills listed here)', 'Major psionic of vast ability: hydrokinesis (super), object read, mind block, resist fatigue, resist hunger, plus three physical powers of choice', '5 to 6 feet (1.5-1.8 m)', '200 to 300 lbs (90-135 kg)', '160 Earth years', 'The world''s oceans, especially the North/South Atlantic, Mediterranean, Black Sea, Caribbean, Gulf of Mexico, Indian Ocean, and Arabian Sea; live aboard ships, rarely on land', 'Atlantis/the Splugorth (trade, safe harbor); other horune pirate crews and Fleet Commanders; other pirates, villains, and evildoers (deals)', 'the New Navy/Nemo-2 (frequent clashes, rescue slaves); Tritonia''s shipping (raided, though the island itself is untouched); surface dwellers and aquatic D-bees generally (viewed as prey); naut''yll (rivals for control of the seas, though some renegades join the horune)', 'Most take a standard pirate R.C.C. path; 1-in-1,000 is a Ship Dreamer (alien mystic shipbuilder, detailed separately, not extracted here); a horune may instead choose the Mystic O.C.C.', 'Five-eyed, avian-descended D-bee raiders who dominate the world''s oceans as brutal, mega-damage pirates loosely allied with the Splugorth of Atlantis.', 'Rifts World Book 7: Underseas p.164-165');




